<title>UK: GKN Westland buys BP aerospace unit.</title>
<headline>GKN Westland buys BP aerospace unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering group GKN Plc said on Wednesday its unit GKN Westland Aerospace had agreed to buy BP Chemicals Advanced Materials Division for around 9.0 million stg from British Petroleum Co Plc.</p>
<p>BP Chemicals Advanced Materials Division designs, develops and makes composite structures for the aerospace industry. Sales in 1996 totalled 14.6 million stg and the company employs 280 people.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
